solutions.latex:
\exfigure{271_q33_s1}

In triangle $OAB$, $OA = 20$, $OB = 50$ and $\angle AOB = 45^\circ$, so use the cosine rule.
$$\begin{aligned} AB^2 &= 50^2 + 20^2 - 2\times 20\times 50\cos 45^\circ \\ &= 1485.78\ldots \\ AB &= 38.5 \text{ km (to 1 decimal place)} \end{aligned}$$

